// Pull request author: popkir
// Change: new rule
// Title: Contagious Interview Implant Run Key Persistence
// Sigma ID: 228eadd9-591b-411c-949d-8baeb92df78d
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Kirill Popov
// Date: 2026-10-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1547.001, execution, T1059.005
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects the HKCU Run values registered by the components of a DPRK "Contagious Interview" chain.
//   The Node.js implant uses "reg.exe add" to set "Microsoft Realtime Aggregator" to "wscript.exe
//   <home>\.vs_cache\main.vbs" for itself and "SettingSyncResCache" to "wscript.exe
//   <...>\Win32\ResCache\nsm-launch.vbs" for the NetSupport client it installs; the native
//   PrintHost.exe collector sets "PrintSpoolHost" to its own path with "--background". On the
//   operator self-delete command (ss_del) the implant deletes its own value and the names
//   "NvidiaDriverUpdate", "VScode.Update.Publisher" and "Microsoft Realtime Agreegator" (likely
//   earlier builds); the misspelt one is kept here.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.ic3.gov/CSA/2026/260918.pdf
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/761e0adb34e6f89ba43fcd65cf861593bfee9319e38e6175394921309e83a254
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/365315e31354b811f8ea537417ff4e0938862a409be434c9a3ff821d57dff384
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/fa23002b3c18ef5eb6ee47ceedde81228ebef016/rules-emerging-threats/2026/TA/Contagious-Interview/registry_set_mal_contagious_interview_run_key_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run.*$" and ((RegistryKey endswith "\\SettingSyncResCache" or RegistryKey endswith "\\Microsoft Realtime Aggregator" or RegistryKey endswith "\\Microsoft Realtime Agreegator" or RegistryKey endswith "\\PrintSpoolHost") or (RegistryValueData contains "\\.vs_cache\\main.vbs" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Win32\\ResCache\\nsm-launch.vbs" or RegistryValueData contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PrintHost\\PrintHost.exe"))
